ea unverified.\n\n## QA sweep summary (AnkiDroid, current build)\n\n**Bugs filed (2, both confirmed by the developer):**\n\n1. **Tag checkbox shows a wrong state with mixed selection.** With comer (tagged `verb`) and mesa (untagged) selected, the Edit tags dialog shows `verb` fully checked. Selecting mesa alone shows it unchecked, and comer alone shows it checked. The mixed case should be a partial/indeterminate state. It looks like the checkbox is driven by the union of the selected rows' tags, not by how many of them have the tag. I saw the same thing with comer + bonjour across decks.\n2. **Browser opens on the wrong deck when launched from a deck's \"Browse cards\".** After the browser was last left on Spanish, \"Browse cards\" from French opened on Spanish with 4 cards. The saved browser state overrode the launching request. The reverse case (Spanish request while saved state was French) opened on Spanish correctly.\n\n**Checked and looks correct:**\n- Browser opens on the last-used deck; deck dropdown switches to French (bonjour, chat, pain) and Spanish.\n- Rotating the browser to landscape and back keeps the list intact.\n- Search of all decks returns 7 cards.\n- Tag dialog: single-note states are correct, the tag filter (\"zz\" shows nothing), and Check/uncheck all toggles the single tag. I cancelled every tag dialog, so no tag data changed.\n- Deck picker \"Filter decks\": \"S\" → All decks + Spanish; \"Sx\" → no match; delete back to \"S\" restores the result; \"Fr\" → French only; lowercase \"spanish\" matches.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- **Deck-list expand/collapse arrows.** Spanish and French have no subdecks, so there are no arrows to test. Testing it needs a parent deck, which means creating a subdeck. The preconditions don't include one, so I didn't change the collection.\n- **\"%\" in the filter box.** It echoed as \"%%\" for me, but the developer could not reproduce it, so I did not file it.\n\n**Decision for you:** Should I create a test subdeck under Spanish to exercise the expand/collapse arrows? That changes the collection (I would delete the subdeck afterward). Once that's done I can finish the sweep and sign off.", "ttft_ms": 1342, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 231678, "uuid": "ec2b6790-1c3e-4768-99b6-617cda0259be", "ttft_stream_ms": 1127, "time_to_request_ms": 447, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 4, "system_prompt": 8, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 2, "conversation_append": 0, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "init_frame_send": 2, "engine_pickup": 1, "loop_entry": 2, "message_prep": 0, "model_config_wait": 1, "autocompact": 1, "request_announcements": 3, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 405, "tool_schema_build": 3, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 2, "request_build": 3}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_to_request_loop_lag_ms": 2, "time_to_request_cpu_ms": 173, "time_to_request_major_faults": 0, "input_attachments_detail": {"slowest_producer": "model", "slowest_producer_ms": 0, "cpu_ms": 5, "major_faults": 0, "setup_ms": 0, "prompt_producers_ms": 0, "ambient_start_ms": 1, "ambient_wait_ms": 0, "render_ms": 0, "producers": 43, "token_counts": 0}, "tool_schema_build_detail": {"betas_ms": 0, "waits_ms": 1, "placement_ms": 0, "render_ms": 1, "after_ms": 0, "other_ms": 1, "tools": 12, "new_schemas": 12}, "message_normalization_detail": {"before_ms": 0, "normalize_ms": 1, "images_ms": 0, "post_process_ms": 0, "after_ms": 0, "other_ms": 0, "messages": 9, "wire_messages": 2}, "request_build_detail": {"records_ms": 0, "system_ms": 1, "headers_ms": 0, "cache_break_record_ms": 1, "plans_ms": 0, "retry_setup_ms": 0, "sent_build_ms": 1, "record_attempt_ms": 0, "other_ms": 0, "sent_build_safety_context_ms": 0, "sent_build_cache_breakpoints_ms": 0, "sent_build_surrogate_scan_ms": 0}, "first_content_frame_ms": 1127, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "model_usage_since_last_result": {"claude-haiku